    "difficulty": {
      ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
    "problem_before": "For $0\\le t\\le 8,$ the equation ${q}^{\u2032}(t)=0$ has at least{{field-1}}\nsolution(s).",
    "worked_solution_before": "The solutions to ${q}^{\u2032}(t)=0$ correspond to the stationary points of the graph of $q(t).$\n\nSketching a possible graph of $q(t),$ we get the following:\n\n![](images/2f/2fd9e08520f4a671a255f360e583140175650de856a12233962c99a064c4c582.png)\n\nFrom our sketch, we notice three stationary points located near $t=2,$ $t=3,$ and $t=4.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${q}^{\u2032}(t)=0$ has at least three solutions.",
    "learner_uses": [],
    "commit_status": "not_submitted",
    "decision": "retain_entry",
    "reason": "Existing numerical entry structure is not a finite-subset radio task."
  },
