    "problem_before": "![](images/19/1915c74f3364314b284b37b6f0f4b31621f981d702966c8a7da1a3b63abb2179.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=g(x)$ is plotted above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the point where ${g}^{\u2032}(x)=0?$\n\n${g}^{\u2032}(x)=0$ when $x\\,=$\n{{field-1}}",
    "worked_solution_before": "A stationary point of $g(x)$ is a value of $x$ where ${g}^{\u2032}(x)=0.$ Graphically, those are the values where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.  \n\nIn the given graph, we can see that at $x=-1,$  the tangent to the graph is horizontal, so we have ${g}^{\u2032}(x)=0$ at this point.\n\n![](images/53/53b00f9b6ff275b7575ad05e608d4d71afe7ef383a37b9e9f8c68117d778a149.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, there is one stationary point, and its $x$-coordinate is $x=-1.$",
    "learner_uses": [],
    "commit_status": "not_submitted",
    "decision": "retain_entry",
    "reason": "Existing numerical entry structure is not a finite-subset radio task."
  },
