    "difficulty": {
      ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
    "problem_before": "The function $f(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,5].$ It has a global maximum and a global minimum both at critical points inside the interval $x\\in (-3,5).$ Which of the following could be the graph of $f(x)?$",
    "worked_solution_before": "The correct answer is shown below:\n\n![](images/c3/c34e392e42337d58cd0ea1f8fe94050a8931f3413bf1b749c4546bfa8a1e2d67.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The global maximum is located at the point marked as $A,$ which is a critical point of $f(x)$ that lies inside $(-3,5).$ Note that ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=0$ at this point.\n\n- The global minimum is located at the point marked as $B,$ which is a critical point of $f(x)$ that lies inside $(-3,5).$ Note that ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ does not exist at this point (corner).",
    "learner_uses": [],
    "commit_status": "not_submitted",
    "decision": "retain_radio",
    "reason": "Single whole-graph alternatives, not combination options or a requested finite subset; retain the existing single-graph response contract."
